OL,3,ABBC apologises for 'any offence caused'
OL,4,Aby Strictly noise disruption
OL,5,
OL,6,FAt the end of the programme, presenter
OL,7,FEmma Willis apologised to viewers "if
OL,8,Fyou heard any audio disruptions". A BBC
OL,9,Fspokesperson also issued an apology and
OL,10,Fsaid it was "investigating how this
OL,11,Fhappened".
OL,13,FLancashire police said it was assessing
OL,14,Fwhether any criminal offences may have
OL,15,Ftaken place, after receiving a formal
OL,16,Fcomplaint and a mobile phone being
OL,17,Fseized.
OL,23,APub: 22-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/38
